Checkpoint 9 owner validation - Fintraffic ingestion
====================================================

Status: completed and accepted by the repository owner on 2026-07-23.

Prerequisites
-------------

- Checkpoint 8 discovery has populated active `fin` streams.
- PostgreSQL and local Mosquitto are running.
- `.env` contains the S3 configuration and a meaningful
  `FINTRAFFIC_USER_HEADER`. Never print that value.

1. Focused automated tests
--------------------------

    uv run --env-file .env pytest -q \
      tests/ingestion/fintraffic \
      tests/ingestion/windy \
      tests/ingestion/shared \
      tests/metrics \
      tests/storage \
      tests/worker

Confirm that the bulk snapshot, null marker, changed image, metadata/image race,
zero-retry, transformation, durable publication, metrics, and worker tests pass.

Recorded result after the final observability additions:

    43 passed, 1 skipped

2. Bounded read-only provider test
----------------------------------

    just ingest-fintraffic --limit 10 --dry-run

Confirm that one bulk snapshot is reported, no more than ten registered streams
are selected, provider markers are ISO timestamps, and no S3/MQTT write occurs.

Recorded result: successful. The live snapshot contained approximately 2,263
to 2,264 usable markers during validation; selected images downloaded,
validated, and transformed without external writes.

3. Bounded publication and registry uniqueness
-----------------------------------------------

Ensure the host-published PostgreSQL and MQTT services are running:

    just infrastructure

    just ingest-fintraffic --limit 4 --publish

Confirm that changed images are validated, transformed, stored, and published.
Do not use a second immediate bounded command as an idempotency test: streams
that have never downloaded successfully remain due, while successful streams
become temporarily not due, so the two samples need not contain the same
cameras. Marker comparison, deterministic image IDs, and collision rejection
are exercised by the automated tests. The continuous worker additionally
enforces its 15-second minimum epoch period, which this one-shot command does
not. The just recipe runs Python on the host and therefore selects
`127.0.0.1` for the local Mosquitto broker rather than the Docker-internal
hostname `mqtt`.

Recorded result: successful. A bounded image completed validation, T0V0
transformation, EWC S3 upload, durable outbox completion, and QoS 1 MQTT
publication.

4. Parallel monitored worker
----------------------------

    just ingestion-test-fintraffic 20m staggered

The recipe prints the unique screen session and log path. Tunnel Grafana port
3000 and open the Fintraffic ingestion dashboard. Confirm:

- Prometheus target `fintraffic-worker-host-benchmark` is up on port 8014;
- initial releases span the configured 600-second window;
- one provider freshness snapshot is made per non-empty epoch;
- metrics have `source_network="fin"` and do not merge with Windy;
- freshness and download retry counts are zero unless explicitly overridden;
- changed jobs expose relevant transformation, image size/dimensions, S3,
  MQTT, source-job duration, derived-image count, and provider latency metrics.

Recorded result: successful. The accepted 20-minute run completed 60 epochs and
27,910 jobs, published 5,555 images, applied all 3,505 eligible EMA candidates,
and observed no throttling, S3 failure, or MQTT failure. The persistent
download-error volume was traced primarily to 85 never-successful provider
cameras repeatedly remaining due; this is documented as a possible later
backoff/status refinement rather than a checkpoint blocker.

The Windy and Fintraffic dashboards are explicitly filtered by
`source_network`, and source/derived metadata plus one-minute external-download
and successful-S3-PUT throughput metrics are present. A newly started worker is
required after metric-code changes because an already running process cannot
expose newly defined collectors.

Checkpoint 9 is accepted. The optional one-hour convergence benchmark is
follow-up performance analysis and does not block checkpoint 10.
